@startuml
title Room Housekeeping & Operational State Machine (v0.9.0)

[*] --> Inspected : Room created & verified\n(is_active = true)

state "Dirty" as Dirty : Needs cleaning\nNot eligible for assignment
state "Clean" as Clean : Cleaned by housekeeping\nAwaiting supervisor inspection\nNot eligible for assignment
state "Inspected" as Inspected : Verified ready\nEligible for guest assignment (FR-OP-03)
state "Occupied" as Occupied : Active stay (CheckedIn)\nRoom locked from reassignment
state "Out-of-Order" as OOO : Maintenance / unavailable\nExcluded from immediate check-in

Dirty --> Clean : markClean()\n[Housekeeping Staff]
Clean --> Inspected : markInspected()\n[Supervisor / Manager]
Clean --> Dirty : Failed inspection / Re-soiled\n[Supervisor / Housekeeping]

Inspected --> Occupied : Guest checks in\n[Front Desk: Inspected & active only]
Occupied --> Dirty : Guest checks out\n[System Auto-Transition]

Dirty --> OOO : markOutOfOrder(reason)\n[Manager / Maintenance]
Clean --> OOO : markOutOfOrder(reason)\n[Manager / Maintenance]
Inspected --> OOO : markOutOfOrder(reason)\n[Manager / Maintenance]

OOO --> Dirty : resolveMaintenance()\n[Must be cleaned & inspected before reuse]

Inspected --> [*] : deactivateRoom()\n[is_active = false]
Dirty --> [*] : deactivateRoom()\n[is_active = false]
OOO --> [*] : deactivateRoom()\n[is_active = false]

note right of Inspected
  Assignment Rule (FR-OP-03):
  Only rooms in Inspected state
  with is_active = true and no
  overlapping stay can be assigned.
end note
@enduml
